# ==============================================================================
# AI Project Reviewer - frontend environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` only if you need to override a default.
#
# NEVER put a secret in this file, or in any VITE_ variable. Vite inlines every
# VITE_-prefixed value into the JavaScript bundle at build time, which means it
# is readable by anyone who opens the page. The GitHub token and every other
# credential stay server-side, in backend/.env, and are never sent to the
# browser.
# ==============================================================================

# Base URL the browser uses for API calls. `/v1/<endpoint>` is appended to it,
# so "/api" becomes "/api/v1/health".
#
#   Local development      "/api"
#     Vite proxies /api to the backend on :8000 (see vite.config.js), so the
#     browser makes same-origin requests and CORS never enters into it.
#
#   Single-host production "/api"
#     Frontend and API behind one reverse proxy or one domain. Still
#     same-origin, still no CORS. This is the simplest deployment.
#
#   Split-host production  "https://api.your-domain.com/api"
#     Frontend on a static host, API elsewhere. The API's CORS_ORIGINS must
#     then list this frontend's exact origin, and the API must be served over
#     HTTPS - a browser on an HTTPS page will block a plain-HTTP API call.
#
# This value is baked in at build time, not read at runtime: change it and
# rebuild.
VITE_API_BASE_URL="/api"
